# ============================================================
#  What never goes into the image
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#  vendor/ is the one that matters. The Dockerfile installs
#  dependencies before copying the application, so that a code
#  change does not reinstall them — and then `COPY . /app` would
#  put a developer's own vendor/ straight over the top of the one
#  just installed, replacing a verified --no-dev tree with
#  whatever happened to be on a laptop, including dev packages.
#
#  .env is here because secrets belong in the platform, not in a
#  layer that anybody who can pull the image can read.
# ============================================================

vendor/
node_modules/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Nothing the running site needs
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Local artefacts
*.log
*.sql.gz
public/uploads/*
!public/uploads/.htaccess
